== JWT signing key strength

HMAC JWTs rely on a secret key to sign and verify tokens. A short or predictable key can be recovered
with an offline dictionary attack, allowing an attacker to forge claims.

=== Assignment

The sample token is signed with a random 256-bit key generated by the server. Submit it unchanged to
verify its signature. Then change a claim and submit the modified token; signature verification
must reject it. A key with this much entropy cannot be recovered with a practical dictionary
attack. Production signing keys should be managed outside source code and rotated through trusted
configuration. The token expires after one minute, so request a fresh sample if needed.
